Trota OS Kiosk
==============

The first screen shows one web page, full screen, in Firefox (kiosk mode)
inside the cage Wayland compositor. The browser starts at boot, comes back by
itself if it crashes or is closed, and is restarted every day at 04:00.

Configuration: /etc/trota-kiosk.conf
  TROTA_KIOSK_URL=https://example.com/board   page to show
  TROTA_KIOSK_VT_SWITCH=no                     yes = allow Ctrl+Alt+F<n>
Apply: sudo systemctl restart trota-kiosk

Firefox policies (no updates prompts, no telemetry, no password manager...):
/etc/firefox/policies/policies.json. Every start uses a fresh, empty profile.

Administration: SSH with keys, or the serial console. Provision many screens
with cloud-init (NoCloud data source on a USB drive labelled CIDATA), e.g.:

  #cloud-config
  ssh_authorized_keys: [ "ssh-ed25519 AAAA... admin" ]
  write_files:
    - path: /etc/trota-kiosk.conf
      content: |
        TROTA_KIOSK_URL=https://intranet.example/board
  runcmd: [ [systemctl, restart, trota-kiosk] ]
